WEBVTT

00:00:00.014 --> 00:00:04.577
We will start by asking why a workload might need distributed processing.

00:00:04.577 --> 00:00:08.322
Then we will introduce the Spark execution model.

00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:14.887
After that, we will connect SQL and DataFrames, discuss lakehouse and Delta concepts,

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:17.967
and practice familiar SQL patterns.

00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:23.952
The last part of the module focuses on query plans, partitions, shuffles, and project-style reasoning.

00:00:23.952 --> 00:00:30.322
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:36.132
a lakehouse processing millions of web events across many files.

00:00:36.132 --> 00:00:41.597
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:41.597 --> 00:00:45.357
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:45.357 --> 00:00:50.052
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:50.052 --> 00:00:56.347
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:56.347 --> 00:01:00.478
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
